### 4.2.3 MobileCount Architecture Specification (Dense Specialist)

**Design Philosophy:**

MobileCount is designed to operate as the high-capacity path of the hybrid system for dense crowd scenes. The architecture leverages the computational efficiency and generalisation capability of a pretrained MobileNetV2 encoder, extended with dilated convolution context blocks for multi-scale feature extraction and a skip-connection fusion module for spatial detail recovery. The model is deployed in knowledge-distilled form, having been trained to replicate the density estimation behaviour of the CSRNet teacher; the teacher is excluded from the deployed pipeline.

**Architecture Overview:**

The encoder is implemented using the MobileNetV2 feature extraction layers split into two stages. Stage 1 (backbone.features[0:7]) produces a spatial feature map at 1/8 of the input resolution with 32 channels — this is retained as the skip connection. Stage 2 (backbone.features[7:14]) further processes the features to produce a 1/16-resolution, 96-channel representation. Three dilated convolution blocks (each: Conv3×3 with dilation=2, batch normalisation, ReLU; 96→96 channels) extract multi-scale contextual information at the 1/16-resolution level. The processed features are upsampled by factor 2 to match the Stage 1 skip resolution (1/8), then concatenated with the skip connection to form a 128-channel combined representation. A fusion module (Conv3×3 (128→64) + BN + ReLU + Conv3×3 (64→32) + BN + ReLU) integrates the combined features. The output head (Conv1×1 (32→1) + ReLU) produces the final density map at 1/8 input resolution. For a 384×384 input, the output is 48×48; the crowd count is derived by summing all spatial values.

The detailed specification of the CSRNet teacher (used during distillation only) is provided in Table 4.4 for reference.

---

**[Table 4.3 — MobileCount Architecture Specification]**

| Component | Configuration | Output Shape | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Input | RGB image | B×3×384×384 | Standard resolution |
| **Encoder Stage 1** (features[0:7]) | MobileNetV2 inverted residuals | B×32×48×48 | Stride 8; skip connection source |
| **Encoder Stage 2** (features[7:14]) | MobileNetV2 inverted residuals | B×96×24×24 | Stride 16 |
| **Dilated Context Block 1** | Conv3×3(96→96, dilation=2) + BN + ReLU | B×96×24×24 | Multi-scale context |
| **Dilated Context Block 2** | Conv3×3(96→96, dilation=2) + BN + ReLU | B×96×24×24 | Expanded receptive field |
| **Dilated Context Block 3** | Conv3×3(96→96, dilation=2) + BN + ReLU | B×96×24×24 | |
| Bilinear Upsample ×2 | — | B×96×48×48 | Match Stage 1 resolution |
| **Concat** (skip + upsampled) | — | B×128×48×48 | 32ch + 96ch |
| **Fusion Block** | Conv3×3(128→64)+BN+ReLU + Conv3×3(64→32)+BN+ReLU | B×32×48×48 | Feature integration |
| **Output Head** | Conv1×1(32→1) + ReLU | B×1×48×48 | Density map (1/8 res) |
| **Total Parameters** | | | **≈0.884M** |

*Count = sum(density_map over all spatial positions)*

