**[Table 4.11 — Routing Classifier Training Hyperparameters]**

| Hyperparameter | Value | Justification |
|---|---|---|
| Dataset | NWPU-Crowd (3,109 train, 500 val) | Binary labels from GT count |
| Batch Size | 32 | Classification task |
| Epochs | 25 (early stopping patience = 10) | Rapid convergence |
| Optimizer | Adam | Fine-tuning |
| Learning Rate | 1×10⁻⁴ | Standard |
| Weight Decay | 1×10⁻⁵ | L2 regularisation |
| Loss Function | Cross-Entropy | Binary classification |
| Dropout | p = 0.3 | Prevent overfitting |
| Best Model | Epoch 10 (Val Accuracy: 88.80%) | Highest validation accuracy |

---

### 4.3.3 Experimental Findings and Performance Analysis

#### LCDNet Evaluation

LCDNet was evaluated on the NWPU-Crowd validation set (500 images). The full-set MAE of 348.0 reflects the model's exposure to the entire density range, including dense and extreme-density scenes that are outside its specialised operating regime. On the sparse stratum (images with GT count ≤ 100, n = 181), LCDNet achieves an MAE of 21.5, demonstrating strong performance within its designated density range. Table 4.12 summarises the LCDNet performance metrics.

**[Table 4.12 — LCDNet Performance Metrics — NWPU-Crowd Validation Set]**

| Metric | Full Val Set (n=500) | Sparse Only (n=181, count ≤100) |
|---|---|---|
| MAE | 348.0 | **21.5** |
| RMSE | 1,033.9 | — |
| Inference Time (GPU) | 23.1 ms | — |
| Inference Time (CPU) | 208.8 ms | — |
| GPU Peak Memory | 368.8 MB | — |
| GFLOPs | 14.59 | — |
| Parameters | 0.917M | — |

*Note: The high full-set MAE is expected — LCDNet is the sparse specialist and is only invoked for images with count ≤ 100 in the hybrid system.*

