#### Routing Classifier Evaluation

The routing classifier was trained to perform binary scene classification (sparse / dense) enabling adaptive model selection in the hybrid system. Table 4.15 summarises the training dynamics at selected epochs, and Table 4.16 provides the final performance metrics.

**[Table 4.15 — Routing Classifier Training Dynamics (Selected Epochs)]**

| Epoch | Train Loss | Train Acc (%) | Val Loss | Val Acc (%) | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 0.4086 | 80.48 | 0.2887 | 87.60 | Rapid initial learning |
| 5 | 0.0944 | 96.62 | 0.3810 | 87.00 | Training accuracy improving |
| **10** | **0.0125** | **99.61** | **0.5096** | **88.80** | **Best validation accuracy** |
| 15 | 0.0114 | 99.65 | 0.6424 | 87.40 | Validation plateauing |
| 20 | 0.0072 | 99.71 | 0.5792 | 86.80 | Training complete |

**[Table 4.16 — Routing Classifier Final Performance Metrics]**

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Best Validation Accuracy | 88.80% (Epoch 10) |
| Expected Calibration Error (ECE, 10-bin) | 0.095 |
| GPU Inference Latency | 4.8 ms/image |
| CPU Inference Latency | 8.9 ms/image |
| GPU Peak Memory | 52.6 MB |
| Parameters | 2.552M |
| GFLOPs | 0.33 |
| Routing Threshold T | 100 (GT count) |

**Confusion Matrix (NWPU-Crowd val, 500 images):**

| | Predicted Sparse | Predicted Dense |
|---|---|---|
| **Actual Sparse (n=181)** | 161 (88.9%) | 20 (11.1%) |
| **Actual Dense (n=319)** | 36 (11.3%) | 283 (88.7%) |

Performance metrics: Precision (sparse): 81.7%, Recall (sparse): 88.9%, Precision (dense): 93.4%, Recall (dense): 88.7%, F1-Score: 88.8%.

The gap between training accuracy (99.71%) and validation accuracy (88.80%) by epoch 20 suggests some overfitting. However, the strong validation performance confirms that the router generalises effectively to unseen images. Classification errors are concentrated near the routing boundary (counts between approximately 80 and 120 individuals) where image complexity is inherently ambiguous.

